{
  "title": "Pseudogout (CPPD)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/basic-science/7040/pseudogout-cppd",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 17 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pseudogout is a common form of inflammatory arthritis caused by intra-articular calcium pyrophosphate dihydrate crystal deposition and presents with attacks of joint pain, joint stiffness and swelling.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made by joint aspiration and crystal analysis showing weakly positively birefringent rhomboid-shaped crystals",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually medical management with NSAIDs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "commonly affects the elderly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rarely affects younger patients, unless occurring in conjunction with other disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "hemochromatosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hyperparathyroidism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "SLE",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "gout",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "RA",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Wilson's disease",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hemophilia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "long term hemodialysis can cause a pyrophosphate like deposition disorder",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chondrocalcinosis is present in 7% of patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Mimics gout except",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects **older patients** > 60 years old",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "affects more **proximal joints**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "positively-birefringent crystal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "acute, onset joint tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "warm, erythematous joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly on knee (most common) and wrist joints (2nd most common)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "erythematous, monoarticular arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "joints tender to palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may observe superficial mineral deposits under the skin at affected joints",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may see calcification of fibrocartilage structures (**chondrocalcinosis**)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "TFCC in wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7040/images/screen_shot_2017-04-10_at_8.05.15_pm.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "meniscus in the knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7040/images/chondrocalcinosis%20knee_moved.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Evaluation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Joint aspiration crystal analysis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**weakly positively birefringent rhomboid-shaped crystals**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7040/images/8ae1c165-a60d-4c68-b6af-28937160d927_pseudogout..jpg",
                  "caption": "Crystal analysis showing weakly positive birefringent rhomboid-shaped crystals consistent with Pseudogout"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Acute pseudogout**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**NSAIDS**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**splint**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**intra-articular steroids**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**splints for comfort**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Chronic pseudogout**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "nonoperative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**intraarticular yttrium-90 injections**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**colchicine (** 0.6 mg PO bid for recurrent cases)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "prophylactic colchine can help to prevent recurrence",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Can result in permanent damage to the joints and renal disease",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
